      "side": 1,
      "message": "The request is allocated with maxReqSize (7, or 11 for a 1.3 terminus) and the whole buffer is sent (L290), but only payloadLength bytes are encoded. Smaller data sizes therefore carry trailing zero bytes; for example, a uint32 effecter on a 1.3 terminus sends 11 bytes instead of 7. Per DSP0248 1.3.0 Table 48, the request length follows effecterDataSize, and a strict responder may reject the extra bytes. Suggest request.resize(sizeof(pldm_msg_hdr) + payloadLength); after encoding.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 245,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 245,
        "endChar": 4
      },
